 "showTitle": "The Hard Saying",
 "title": "Sometime",
 "dates": "Monday, December 14 – Saturday, December 19, 2009",
 "logline": "Finals week: twenty minutes inside somebody else’s argument, one in the morning in a car with no future — and the last night, every place it happened, until the shuttle comes.",
 "previously": [
  {
   "text": "In a drugstore aisle at half past one in the morning: “Where do you go, Jack?” “I’ll tell you sometime. Not yet.” “Okay.”",
   "if": "lena_sometime"
  },
  {
   "text": "Under Theo’s mistletoe Julian kissed her cheek. It was the only time all night you let yourself look, and her eyes came straight to you.",
   "if": "e21_glance"
  },
  {
   "text": "On Del Playa she took your “right now” apart, point by point. “Is it still right now?” … “A no’s a no. For tonight. For that.”",
   "if": "skye_letter_kept"
  },
  {
   "text": "Father Osei: “…a no that is only for tonight has to be said again tomorrow night, and the night after, to a woman who heard you the first time.”",
   "if": "confessed_skye_2"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the beach at Ellery: “Six days.” “You’re counting.” “I don’t count. I have people who count.”",
   "if": "skye_counting"
  },
  {
   "text": "On Gaudete Sunday you went to breakfast instead of Sully’s. At 1:04 the RAZR buzzed on your desk while you slept: *13. —L.*",
   "if": "missed_saints_13"
  },
  {
   "text": "After the Gaudete Mass she asked the 8-Ball something without moving her lips, and turned it so you could read it: *Better not tell you now.*",
   "if": "lena_has_8ball"
  }
 ],
